<!--
  Build dock, opened by any defense slot's build button: a compact pill that
  floats at one constant height above the clicked slot (BuildPanelSystem sets
  x from the slot, y/z fixed) and yaws to the camera via Billboard(lockY).
  The root is a transparent flex column: a small circular CLOSE button
  centered above a stadium-shaped bar — uniform border-radius = half the bar
  height rounds both side ends — holding one circular icon button per
  placeable unit, icon only: the overlaid live prices were removed (the
  wallet badge above already states the gold, and the glyph kept scattering
  under the digits). Icons are sized 4.5 — the largest the game-icons
  cannon glyph has ever rendered correctly inside the Ø10 circle. Uikit
  containers do not clip children (border-radius is not a mask), and past
  ~5 the cannon glyph scattered into fragments in every file variant
  tried — the original 512-unit path, a scale(0.046875) group wrapper, and
  a script-baked 0..24 path — so the icons sit at the proven 4.5 with the
  cannon restored to its original cannon.svg. The top row centers one dark group — wallet badge and round close
  button side by side (same height 6 and radius, reading as a single
  segmented pill) — instead of pinning the badge to the rim; the badge is
  sized for "9999g", the worst-case wallet, so the digits never resize the
  group. Placement beside the close button rather than under the bar keeps
  the column's total height, and with it the clearance to the
  health bars below, unchanged. The bar is a left-aligned flex row
  and a native uikit scroll
  region (overflow: scroll, scrollbar hidden via scrollbar-width: 0): with
  more placeable units than fit, the extra circles drag in from the right.
  The bar is sized to two and a half button slots (padding 2 + 10 + gap 2 +
  10 + gap 2 + a half button 5 + padding 2 = 33): the tail stays empty while
  only two units exist, and a future third unit renders half-clipped at the
  right rim — the natural drag-me hint. Buttons use the <button> tag
  deliberately: <Panel> pulls the
  horizon kit's glass default (panelMaterialClass globally re-registered as
  GlassMaterial) and washes mid-gray class backgrounds out to white —
  Container (button) renders the class color exactly; the bar itself keeps
  panel-material-class: glass over #ffffffaa to match the pause-menu surface.
  BuildPanelSystem binds the clicks and drives a three-state
  class per unit button: .dock-unit (default), .dock-unit-off (its price
  above the current wallet — dimmed; the number itself is not shown) and
  .dock-unit-hidden (the opened slot holds a live occupant — the whole
  unit row hides, ammo takes the bar) — and rewrites the wallet badge every
  frame while the dock is open, so gold spent or earned elsewhere shows live.
  The ammo row — a global single-select
  (AmmoSelected on the director, rows = AMMO_DEFS) applying to every
  cannon's next shot — renders only over an occupied slot: an empty or
  destroyed one swaps the rows to .ammo-hidden (display none), so build
  and ammo never share the bar. Over an occupied slot the selected round's
  circle keeps the 0.75 open pose and turns brick red #e2574c, while its
  icon grows 4.5→6 (.ammo-icon-active) so the visible red rim around the
  glyph halves to 0.75 — reads as "loaded", not hover. UIKitML stylesheets
  take no descendant selectors, so BuildPanelSystem swaps the icon class
  alongside the row class; v1 ships the free iron ball
  only, so its click is a no-op and the selection never changes. Note
  the stylesheet holds no comments: UIKitML rejects them as selectors.
  Runtime setProperties display would lose to the class layer, so every
  state change must be class-driven. Icons load through the <svg> tag's src
  (uikit Svg component: SVGLoader vector meshes, MeshBasicMaterial,
  tone-mapped off): cannon from the game-icons set, the iron ball and iron
  guard hand-drawn to the same pattern — one path, one #f2f4f7 fill, detail
  cut in as opposite-winding holes. Multi-fill svgs (the old two-tone ball,
  evenodd shield) flicker: each fill becomes its own coplanar mesh and the
  billboard's sort order jitters between frames. State colour lives on the
  disc behind the icon: selected ammo disc goes white #f2f4f7 and its icon
  flips dark through the CSS color override (a white icon would vanish on
  the white disc). Dock-icon srcs carry ?v=<package version> — nginx serves
  ui/ with max-age immutable for a year, so icon edits must bump the query.
  Fills stay
  hardcoded #f2f4f7 because currentColor resolves to black in SVGLoader, and
  src resolves against the page base URL (not the .uikitml location), hence
  the ui/ prefix. Every non-colored container declares background-color
  #00000000: uikit containers default to an opaque white surface. Labels
  stay Latin — the bundled font atlas has no CJK glyph coverage. Dock
  palette: mid-gray #5d646d circles; dark
  gray #3a3f46 close button, matching the
  retired list rows. render-order 18
  keeps the dock under the menu button (20) and above the world overlays
  (health bars 8/9, hit flash 10).
-->
<style>
  .build-dock {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.5;
    width: 33;
    height: 32;
    render-order: 18;
    background-color: #00000000;
  }

  .dock-top {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 2;
    width: 33;
    height: 6;
    background-color: #00000000;
  }

  .wallet-badge {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    width: 12;
    height: 6;
    background-color: #3a3f46;
    border-radius: 3;
  }

  .wallet-text {
    display: flex;
    color: #ffd977;
    font-size: 2.8;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-align: center;
    background-color: #00000000;
  }

  .dock-close {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    width: 6;
    height: 6;
    background-color: #3a3f46;
    color: #ffffff;
    font-size: 3.5;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-align: center;
    border-radius: 3;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .dock-close:hover {
    background-color: #464c55;
  }

  .dock-bar {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: flex-start;
    gap: 2;
    width: 33;
    height: 13;
    padding-left: 2;
    padding-right: 2;
    overflow: scroll;
    scrollbar-width: 0;
    border-radius: 6.5;
    panel-material-class: glass;
    background-color: #ffffffaa;
  }

  .dock-unit {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    width: 10;
    height: 10;
    background-color: #5d646d;
    border-radius: 5;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .dock-unit:hover {
    background-color: #6a717a;
  }

  .dock-unit:active {
    background-color: #515861;
  }

  .dock-unit-off {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    width: 10;
    height: 10;
    background-color: #82878e;
    border-radius: 5;
  }

  .dock-unit-hidden {
    display: none;
  }

  .ammo-unit {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    width: 10;
    height: 10;
    background-color: #5d646d;
    border-radius: 5;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .ammo-unit:hover {
    background-color: #6a717a;
  }

  .ammo-active {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    width: 7.5;
    height: 7.5;
    background-color: #f2f4f7;
    border-radius: 5;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .ammo-icon-active {
    display: flex;
    width: 6;
    height: 6;
    background-color: #00000000;
    color: #2e3440;
  }

  .ammo-hidden {
    display: none;
  }

  .unit-icon {
    display: flex;
    width: 4.5;
    height: 4.5;
    background-color: #00000000;
  }
</style>

<Panel class="build-dock">
  <Panel class="dock-top">
    <button class="wallet-badge">
      <Panel id="wallet-value" class="wallet-text">0g</Panel>
    </button>
    <button id="build-dismiss" class="dock-close">X</button>
  </Panel>
  <Panel class="dock-bar">
    <button id="row-cannon" class="dock-unit">
      <svg class="unit-icon" src="ui/icons/cannon.svg?v=0.1.297" ></svg>
    </button>
    <button id="row-iron-guard" class="dock-unit">
      <svg class="unit-icon" src="ui/icons/iron-guard.svg?v=0.1.297" ></svg>
    </button>
    <button id="ammo-ball-iron" class="ammo-active">
      <svg id="ammo-icon-ball-iron" class="ammo-icon-active" src="ui/icons/ball-iron.svg?v=0.1.297" ></svg>
    </button>
  </Panel>
</Panel>
